ical type. \u000a \u000aNote: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. A stain for \u000aE-cadherin was examined. \u000a \u000a \u000aBREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, few microscopic clusters, two extending to less than \u000a0.1cm from the final margin of the specimen. \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), classical type. \u000a \u000aNote: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen \u000a \u000a \u000aBREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, single microscopic focus, extending to less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the final margin of the specimen. \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), classical type. \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000a \u000aNote: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen \u000a \u000a \u000aBREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, several foci spanning as much as 0.6cm in greatest \u000adimension in tissue section and extending to the final margin of the specimen. \u000a \u000aNote: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. \u000a \u000a \u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy in 2 of 2 lymph nodes. \u000a \u000aNote: Stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin were \u000aexamined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Frederick Carl Koerner MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000a \u000aRESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER-2/c-erbB-2 \u000a \u000aBreast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aHER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is \u000aevaluated visually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA \u000ahas determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory \u000ahas established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 13:28*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aCarcinoma in the left breast \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT \u000aB: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN \u000aF: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL LATERAL MARGIN \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left breast needle localized \u000alumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a \u000alocalization wire. The specimen is inked. It contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm \u000aill-defined, firm, yellow-gray mass containing a barbell clip and a hemorrhagic \u000acavity. The mass abuts the margin and is surrounded by hemorrhagic, chalky \u000ayellow fatty tissue. Representative sections are submitted: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : End margin en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Unremarkable. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : End margin en face. \u000a \u000aB. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left axillary sentinel nodes \u000a#132", are two lymph nodes REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  which are \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left breast final margin \u000asuperior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm piece of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue \u000awith a suture designating the final margin, which is inked. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left breast final margin \u000ainferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm piece of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue \u000awith a suture designating the final margin, which is inked. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left breast final margin \u000amedial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a suture \u000adesignating the final margin, which is inked. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.9cm hemorrhagic nodule, which extends to the final margin, surrounded by \u000achalky yellow foci. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aF. Unfixed, labeled "Nancy Lattanzio, REMOVED_DATE  left breast final margin \u000alateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm piece of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with \u000aa suture designating the final margin, which is inked. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT \u000aPART B: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA \u000aPART C: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN \u000aPART D: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN \u000aPART E: BREAST EXCIS