VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 61) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: Same Day Surgery Unit \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 11:46 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichelle Connolly Specht MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT: \u000a- Invasive ductal carcinoma, see table #1. \u000a- Ductal carcinoma in-situ. \u000a- Focal flat epithelial atypia. \u000a- Fibrocystic changes. \u000a- Healing biopsy site. \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000a \u000aTumor Size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  \u000aGrade: 2. \u000aLymphatic Vessel Invasion: Present, a few foci. \u000aBlood Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aMargin of Invasive Carcinoma: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or \u000agreater. \u000aLocation of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: Within the region of the mass. \u000aGrade of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: 2. \u000aMargin of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm \u000aor greater. \u000aStains for Receptors: Requested. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT FINAL MARGIN LATERAL: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aC. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aD. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR: \u000a- Focal flat epithelial atypia. \u000a \u000aE. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT FINAL MARGIN DEEP: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aF. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aG. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA # 378: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy in 4 lymph nodes (0/4). \u000a \u000aNOTE: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and wide \u000aspectrum keratin were examined on tissue levels of the sentinel lymph node (Part \u000aG). The resection margins of the breast specimens were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated (Parts A-F). \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000a \u000aQUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is \u000aevaluated visually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membran