nancy. \u000a \u000aC. RIGHT MEDIASTINAL LYMPH NODE EXCISION: \u000aReactive lymph node. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aNote: This case does not contain all the coding components for CMS PQRI measure \u000a#99. \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Kristina M Braaten MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aRight breast cancer; status post lumpectomy with close margins. Right \u000amastectomy with flap reconstruction. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aB: SKIN EXCISION, RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP \u000aC: LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT MEDIASTINAL \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "right breast", is a \u000a22.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 4.1cm simple mastectomy specimen oriented with a short suture \u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is \u000aanteriorly surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm portion of skin with a central 2.5cm in \u000adiameter areolar complex exhibiting a central everted nipple. The specimen is \u000ainked as follows: anterior blue, posterior black. Cut section shows the \u000aspecimen contains in the 12:00 position a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.3cm biopsy cavity which \u000aextends through the anterior surgical margin and to within 1.2cm of the \u000aposterior surgical margin. The specimen also contains, in the inner lower \u000aquadrant, a rubbery tan-white homogeneous circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm \u000anodule extending to 0.2cm of the anterior and 1.3cm of the posterior surgical \u000amargins. The remaining cut surfaces are composed of tan-yellow fibrofatty \u000atissue mottled with areas of dense fibrous tissue. No lymph nodes are palpated \u000ain the upper-outer quadrant. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 12:00 biopsy site closest anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 12:00 biopsy site. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 12:00 biopsy site closest posterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-inner quadrant rubbery nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-inner quadrant fibrous tissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer quadrant fibrous tissue. \u000a \u000aThe specimen was re-examined, and diffuse firm tissue (but without a discrete \u000alesion) was identified in the upper outer and lateral aspects of the breast. \u000aAdditional sections were subsequently submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral breast \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer contiguous sections \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer contiguous sections \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer breast \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-inner breast (JS) \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "right mastectomy \u000askin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm circular piece of skin and soft tissue with a \u000acentral REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm hole. No masses or lesions are seen. Representative \u000asections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . (DK) \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "right mediastinal \u000alymph node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm tan-pink lymph node, which is submitted in \u000atoto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . (DK) \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aPART B: SKIN EXCISION, RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP \u000aPART C: LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT MEDIASTINAL \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
