ed and frozen entirely \u000aas FX#1, now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Packaged fatty tissue is entirely \u000asubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh in the frozen section lab labeled "right axillary sentinel \u000anode", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-pink lymph node with scanty amount of \u000aattached fatty tissue. The fatty tissue is separated. The lymph node is \u000abisected and frozen entirely as FX#1, now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Packaged \u000afatty tissue is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a(HG) \u000a \u000aThe specimen is received in 8 containers which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , \u000aREMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aC. The specimen is received fresh, labeled "right breast" is a 22 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm nipple sparing mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the \u000asuperior and a long suture designating lateral. The anterior margin is inked \u000ablue and the posterior margin inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.8cm ill-defined, indurated, nodular tan-gray mass within the central, upper \u000aouter quadrant which extends to the anterior margin to 2.5cm of the posterior \u000amargin. The mass contains a S-shaped metallic clip. The surrounding tissue is \u000atan-yellow, fibrofatty and diffusely nodular. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm \u000aill-defined, rubbery, nodular mass with a central, chalky yellow and hemorrhagic \u000afocus within the central breast (mass #2) which is 1.5cm from the anterior \u000amargin, 6cm from the posterior margin and separated from mass #1 by 8.5cm of \u000afibrofatty tissue. No clip is identified. The surrounding tissue is gray-white \u000ato tan-yellow fibrofatty with focal soft, pink nodular areas and cystic areas. \u000aLymph nodes are not seen in the lateral tissue. The following representative \u000asections are s