VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  JOYCE E. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 45) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 09:02 \u000aResults To: \u000aJonathan Michael Winograd MD \u000aKevin S. Hughes MD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. BREAST BIOPSY, LEFT NIPPLE CORE: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000aFibroadenoma (1.0cm ), involved by LCIS. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia. \u000aClip grossly identified. (See note.) \u000a \u000aNote: No histologic features definitive for a biopsy site are seen on the \u000aslides, but a clip was grossly identified and the clip site was entirely \u000asubmitted for microscopic evaluation. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA 827: \u000aNo evidence of carcinoma in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000apankeratin were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. BREAST BIOPSY, RIGHT NIPPLE: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aE. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multifocal. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia. \u000aLobular neoplasia (atypical lobular hyperplasia). \u000aFibrocystic changes, including complex sclerosing lesion. \u000aFibroadenoma (0.6cm ). \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000a \u000a \u000aF. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA 622: \u000aNo evidence of carcinoma in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000apankeratin were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a \u000aG. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA 189: \u000aNo evidence of carcinoma in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000apankeratin were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Amy Ly MD*** \u000a \u000aResident Pathologist: \u000aSarah E. Johnstone MD \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a45 year old female with breast cancer. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST BIOPSY, LEFT NIPPLE CORE \u000aB: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aC: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA 827 \u000aD: BREAST BIOPSY, RIGHT NIPPLE \u000aE: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aF: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA 622 \u000aG: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA 189 \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 7 containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Davidson, unit \u000aREMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "left nipple core", is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of \u000afibroadipose tissue, inked entirely black, bisected and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "left mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.2cm \u000amastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the nipple, a long suture \u000adesignating the lateral aspect and a bowtie suture designating the cephalad \u000aaspect. The anterior margin is inked blue, the nipple area yellow, and the \u000aposterior margin black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm well \u000acircumscribed, tan, lobulated mass that is 1.5cm from the posterior margin and \u000a1.8cm from the anterior margin. A clip is identified adjacent to this mass and \u000ais 2.7cm from the posterior margin and 3.4cm from the anterior margin, in the \u000alower central area. The surrounding tissue is tan-gray and fibrous with \u000amultiple cysts filled with clear fluid, measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0.8cm  No lymph nodes \u000aare detected in the lateral tissue. The following representative sections are \u000asubmitted: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin to mass \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin to mass \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire mass (including entire clip site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Surrounding fibrous area. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant. \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "left sentinel node 827", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm \u000alymph node, bisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "right nipple core", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, inked entirely black, bisected and submitted as \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "right mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.6cm \u000amastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the nipple, a long suture \u000adesignating the lateral aspect and a bowtie designating the cephalad aspect. \u000aThe anterior margin is inked blue, the nipple area yellow, and the posterior \u000amargin black. Serial sectioning reveals a clip adjacent to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm \u000acyst and hemorrhagic fibrous tissue, 3.4cm to the posterior margin and 3.5cm \u000afrom the anterior margin, in the central lower portion. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm \u000atan-gray, well circumscribed nodule is in the central lateral portion, 3.7cm to \u000athe posterior margin and 4.2cm from the anterior margin. The surrounding \u000atissue is fibrous and contains multiple cysts, measuring REMOVED_DATE 6cm in greatest \u000adimension. No lymph nodes are detected in the lateral tissue. Representative \u000asections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous area including clip site. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin to clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin to clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass, central lateral \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional fibrous area surrounding clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central inner fibrous tissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer fibrous tissue. \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "sentinel node 622, right", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000alymph node, bisected and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aG. Received fresh, labeled "right sentinel node 189", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm \u000alymph node, bisected and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining fibroadipose tissue is \u000asubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST BIOPSY, LEFT NIPPLE CORE \u000aPART B: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aPART C: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA 827 \u000aPART D: BREAST BIOPSY, RIGHT NIPPLE \u000aPART E: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
