IAL ATYPIA. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Unfixed in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "Elise Driscoll, REMOVED_DATE  right sentinel lymph node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm lymph node which is bisected, submitted entirely for Frozen as FX #1, and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The fat is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Elise Driscoll, REMOVED_DATE  left axillary node #336", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-pink lymph node, which is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lymph node, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fat. Unfixed, labeled "Elise Driscoll, REMOVED_DATE  right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3.6cm piece of skin with a central unremarkable nipple. A short suture designates the superior aspect, and a long suture designates the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked: posterior black, anterior blue. The specimen consists of lobulated tan-yellow fatty tissue with interspersed dense gray-white fibrous tissue. The fibrous tissue is predominantly located within the upper outer and lower outer quadrants. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral aspect of the specimen. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central aspect of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional tissue. Unfixed, labeled "Elise Driscoll, REMOVED_DATE  left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm left breast simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm piece of skin with a central unremarkable nipple. A short suture designates the superior aspect, and a long suture designates the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked: posterior black, anterior blue. The specimen is sectioned contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm hemorrhagic cavity within the central-inner aspect. The cavity is surrounded by dense gray-white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas and it extends to 1.0cm from the posterior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of lobulated tan-yellow fat with a scant amount of interspersed dense gray-white fibrous tissue. Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral aspect of the specimen. Sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic cavity to the posterior margin.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1; RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: 1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. Some tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do