TIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, ADENOSIS WITH APOCRINE \u000aCYSTS. \u000aHEALING BIOPSY SITE. (SEE NOTE). \u000aNOTE: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated. \u000a \u000aBREAST (RIGHT, DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES, MOSTLY GRADE REMOVED_DATE  \u000aWITH PAGETOID SPREAD, CALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL MUCIN EXTRAVASATION, EXTENSIVELY \u000aINVOLVING ENTIRE SPECIMEN (10 OF 10 BLOCKS, REMOVED_DATE CM), PRESENT AT THE NEW INKED \u000aMARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT. \u000aHEALING BIOPSY SITE. (SEE NOTE). \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical stains (p63, myosin) show that the ductal carcinoma \u000ain-situ is surrounded by myoepithelial cells ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aBREAST (RIGHT, MEDIAL MARGIN), EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, MICROPAPILLARY AND CLINGING TYPES, GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH \u000aFOCAL MUCIN EXTRAVASATION AND PAGETOID SPREAD INVOLVING 7 OF 10 BLOCKS, \u000aSPANNING AT LEAST 4 CM, REMOVED_DATE CM AWAY FROM NEW INKED MARGIN. (SEE NOTE). \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical stains (cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam REMOVED_DATE  p63, myosin and \u000acalponin) were examined ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aBREAST (RIGHT, LATERAL MARGIN), EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES, GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH \u000aCALCIFICATIONS, EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING SPECIMEN (9 OF 10 BLOCKS, AT LEAST 4 CM), \u000aPRESENT AT THE INKED NEW MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT. (SEE NOTE) \u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical stains (cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam REMOVED_DATE  p63, myosin and \u000acalponin) were examined ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aBREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, SOLID, CRIBRIFORM, AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES, GRADE \u000a2-3/3, EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING ENTIRE SPECIMEN (8 OF 8 BLOCKS, REMOVED_DATE CM), PRESENT \u000aAT THE INKED NEW MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT. \u000aNOTE: Few cells suspicious for microinvasion were seen on the hematoxylin-eosin \u000aslides ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). These cells are not represented on immunohistochemical stains \u000a(cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam REMOVED_DATE  p63, myosin and calponin). \u000a \u000aBREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISION: \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES, GRADE REMOVED_DATE  \u000aEXTENSIVELY INVOLVING SPECIMEN (8 OF 11 BLOCKS, AT LEAST 4 CM), PRESENT AT THE \u000aINKED NEW MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT. \u000aHEALING BIOPSY SITE. \u000a \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aReceived are 8 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast inferior atypia", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm \u000alumpectomy specimen, containing a needle localization guidewire, oriented as \u000afollows: Long stitch - lateral, short stitch - superior. The long axis of the \u000aspecimen is the medial-lateral axis, and the specimen is inked as follows: \u000aAnterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow. The \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a \u000awell-circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm hemorrhagic cavity in the lateral portion \u000aof the specimen, located 0.2cm from the lateral tip, 2.5cm from the medial \u000atip, abutting the posterior margin, located 0.4cm from the anterior margin, \u000a0.5cm from the superior margin, and 0.4cm from the inferior margin. No metal \u000aclips are identified. The remainder of the specimen consists predominantly of \u000aunremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely and sequentially \u000asubmitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the lateral tip en face in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the medial tip en face \u000ain  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the hemorrhagic cavity in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast DCIS", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm lumpectomy \u000aspecimen, containing a needle localization guidewire, oriented as follows: \u000aLong stitch - lateral, short stitch - superior. The long axis of the specimen \u000ais the anterior-posterior axis, and the specimen is inked as follows: Superior \u000a- blue, inferior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal predominantly \u000afibroadipose tissue, with scant tan-white fibrous tissue, focal hemorrhage, and \u000aa metal clip located 1.2cm from the anterior tip. The specimen is submitted \u000aas follows: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior tip, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior tip, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area where metal clip was identified. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue immediately posterior to where the metal clip was \u000aidentified. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue posterior to the area where the clip was identified. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of anterior portion of specimen. \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast superior atypia", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm \u000alumpectomy specimen, with a needle localization guidewire, oriented as follows: \u000aLong stitch - lateral, short stitch - superior. The long axis of the specimen \u000ais anterior-posterior axis, and the specimen is inked as follows: Superior - \u000ablue, inferior - black, medial - green, lateral - yellow. The specimen is \u000aserially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal predominantly fleshy, \u000afirm, tan-white, fibrous tissue, with very scant attached fibroadipose tissue, \u000aand focal hemorrhage and disruption running parallel to the anterior-posterior \u000aaxis in the middle of the specimen. No metal clips are identified. There is a \u000aneedle localization guidewire within the specimen. The specimen is entirely \u000asubmitted as follows: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior tip, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior tip, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen, sequentially and entirely submitted from anterior to \u000aposterior. \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast deep margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the \u000anew margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal predominantly fibroadipose tissue, with admixed tan-white \u000afibrous tissue with hemorrhage. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast medial margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the \u000anew margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue, with admixed tan-white to hemorrhagic \u000afibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast lateral margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the \u000anew margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue with scant tan-white fibrous tissue \u000awith focal hemorrhage. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast superior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.6cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the \u000anew margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue and tan-white fibrous tissue with \u000afocal hemorrhage. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived fresh, labeled "right breast inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm \u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented as follows: A stitch indicates the \u000anew margin. The new margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue, with focal tan-white \u000afibrous tissue and hemorrhage, as well as a metal clip, located 0.6cm to the \u000ablack-inked margin. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , with the \u000aarea where the metal clip was identified in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07:17:33PM \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final \u000aDiagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed \u000aor corrected the diagnoses. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aADDENDUM NOTE: \u000aREASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR \u000aPROTEINS \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor \u000aprotein. \u000aThe ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor \u000aprotein. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000aNote: All foci of DCIS represented on the slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  strongly express estrogen \u000areceptor protein. The progesterone receptor expression profile shows some \u000avariation. \u000a \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The \u000aFDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this \u000alaboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aAddendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 14,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:52:20PM \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final \u000aDiagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed \u000aor corrected the diagnoses. \u000a \u000aPART A: Breast (Right Inferior Atypia), Excision \u000aPART B: Breast (Right DCIS), Excision \u000aPART C: Breast (Right Superior Atypia), Excision \u000aPART D: Breast (Right, Deep Margin), Excision \u000aPART E: Breast (Right, Medial Margin), Excision \u000aPART F: Breast (Right, Lateral Margin), Excision \u000aPART G: Breast (Right, Superior \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
