um. To investigate the possibility of metastatic carcinoma, stains for keratin cocktail, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin were performed on three levels of each of six tissue blocks. TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS # 1 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES: 3 (1 sentinel and 2 nonsentinel) TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED: 22 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 2 (nonsentinel) Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 1 (sentinel) Number of lymph nodes with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0 Extracapsular extension: None Other forms of axillary involvement: None GROSS DESCRIPTION: Unfixed, in the Frozen Section Laboratory, labeled "Deborah Stone, REMOVED_DATE  right axillary lymph node biopsy x2", are two pieces of yellow-pink fibroadipose tissue aggregating to 3 x 2 x 1.5cm  The specimen contains a 1.5cm lymph node, which is entirely frozen as FX#1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remainder of the fibroadipose tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Deborah Stone, REMOVED_DATE  right breast mastectomy", is a 22 x 20 x 4.5cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect. The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm skin ellipse appears unremarkable. The everted nipple and areola appear unremarkable. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the posterior margin is inked black. The breast contains three cavities: lateral, spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm  located 1.5cm from the posterior margin and 2.0cm from the anterior margin, and containing serous fluid; medial, spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm  located 1.5cm from the posterior margin and abutting the anterior margin, and containing surgical clips; and inferomedial spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm and located 2.5cm from the posterior margin and 3.5cm from the anterior margin. The remainder of the parenchyma appears nodular around the lateral cavity. In the container is a REMOVED_DATE x 4.o x 0.4cm ellipse of unremarkable skin. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire medial cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire inferomedial cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Additional tissue. In fixative, labeled "Deborah Stone, REMOVED_DATE  right axillary contents", is a 10 x 5 x 2.5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes. The largest spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm  All lymph nodes are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 lymph nodes, 1 inked black and 1 inked blue.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 2 lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 3 lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 4 lymph nodes. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (RIGHT BREAST AXILLARY LYMPH NODE BIOPSY): POSITIVE FOR ADENOCARCINOMA (<0.2 CM). Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on Monday February 08,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:56:24PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node (Right Axilla, Sentinel, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: - Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) - Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) - Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday February 09,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:32:01AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Lymph Node (Right Axilla, Sentinel, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (90) to chromosome 17 signals (88) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. The results at or near the cutoff poi