e biopsy site adjacent to the inferior margin. A small piece of normal \u000afibrous tissue is saved frozen for Tissue Bank. Frozen section will be \u000asubmitted for clinical slide file as per Dr. Andrea Richardson. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Serial resection specimen from lateral to medial aspect with \u000aClip found in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , 9 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, sublabeled "2. Right breast superior margin; stitch, new margin", \u000aconsists of one (1) fragment of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The stitch is placed by the surgeon to designate the new margin. The \u000atissue opposite to the old margin exhibits biopsy changes. The new margin is \u000ainked black, and the old margin is inked blue. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned and entirely submitted for histologic examination. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : New superior margin, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMRU/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a10/24/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
