in, 0.4cm of the nearest lateral margin, 1.0cm from the nearest anterior \u000amargin, and remote (greater than 2.0cm ) from the nearest inferior margin. The \u000ametallic clip is identified within the needle core biopsy cavity at this site. \u000aThe remaining specimen is comprised of focally hemorrhagic fiber-dense tissue \u000a(at least 75%) without additional discrete masses, lesions, or other \u000aabnormalities noted grossly. The entire specimen is submitted sequentially - \u000afrom superior to inferior, with the superior perpendicular margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the \u000ainferior perpendicular margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the majority of lesion in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, multi frags, ESS. \u000aDB/mmm \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a1/6/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
