VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000a55 Fruit Street, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 49) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 13:28 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichelle Connolly Specht MD \u000aChien-Wei Eric Liao MD, PHD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. LEFT BREAST MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Focal flat epithelial atypia. \u000a- Fibrocystic changes with apocrine metaplasia and usual ductal hyperplasia. \u000a- One benign intraparenchymal lymph node. \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #607 EXCISION: \u000a- No carcinoma identified in two lymph nodes (0/2). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 were examined on \u000atissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aE. RIGHT BREAST MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Fibrocystic changes with apocrine metaplasia and usual ductal hyperplasia. \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aF. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #251 EXCISION: \u000a- No carcinoma identified in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 were examined on \u000atissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Travis L Rice-Stitt MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aRecently diagnosed BRCA mutation. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aB: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #607 \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aF: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA #251 \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 6 containers, which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "left mastectomy short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5.0cm nipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a \u000ashort stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The \u000aanterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The \u000aspecimen is composed of grey-white, rubbery, dense and cystic fibrous tissue. A \u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm tan-pink candidate lymph node is identified in the lateral \u000atissue. The specimen was examined by Dr. Travis Rice-Stitt. The following \u000arepresentative sections are submitted: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue, upper outer quadrant, with representative anterior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue, upper inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue, lower inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue, lower outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue, central breast. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Intact candidate lymph node. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "left axillary sentinel node #607," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.0cm aggregate of yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue containing two tan-pink \u000acandidate lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE m in maximum dimension. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Each cassette with one sectioned lymph node. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fibroadipose tissue. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "left subareolar nipple margin," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm piece of yellow-white fibroadipose tissue which is inked black, bisected, \u000aand entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "right subareola nipple margin," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm piece of yellow-white fibroadipose tissue which is inked black, bisected, \u000aand entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . (JBH) \u000a \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "right mastectomy, \u000ashort-superior, long-lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm nipple sparing \u000amastectomy with a short suture designating superior and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin \u000ais inked black. The specimen consists of dense gray-white focally cystic \u000afibrous tissue admixed with soft lobulated adipose tissue. Lymph nodes are not \u000aidentified within the lateral tissue. The specimen is reviewed grossly by Dr. \u000aTravis Rice-Stitt. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant to include posterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant to include anterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast. (JP) \u000a \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "right axillary sentinel node #251," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.8cm tan ovoid candidate lymph node with attached fibroadipose tissue. The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One lymph node, sectioned. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fibroadipose tissue. (JBH) \u000a \u000a \u000aGrossed by: \u000aJennifer Patel \u000aJessica Botelho Houston \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aPART B: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #607 \u000aPART C: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART D: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART E: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
