VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  J. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 57) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: Same Day Surgery Unit \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 20:01 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichelle Connolly Specht MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. BREAST, RIGHT, EXCISION: \u000a1. Invasive ductal carcinoma, with calcifications. \u000a2. Ductal carcinoma in-situ, cribriform type with calcifications. \u000a3. Flat epithelial atypia with associated calcifications. \u000a4. Fibrocystic changes with usual ductal hyperplasia and apocrine cysts, with \u000acalcifications. \u000a5. Healing biopsy site. \u000aSee table #1. \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000a \u000aTumor Size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm (gross measurement). \u000aGrade: 1. \u000aLymphatic Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aBlood Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aMargin of Invasive Carcinoma: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or \u000agreater. \u000aLocation of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: Within and beyond the region of the mass, \u000afew foci. \u000aGrade of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: 2 nuclear grade. \u000aMargin of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm \u000aor greater. \u000aStains for Receptors: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . (Her-2 Only). \u000a \u000aB. BREAST, FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT INFERIOR, EXCISION: \u000aFibrocystic changes with calcifications. Sclerosing adenosis. Microscopic \u000aradial scar. (See note). \u000aNOTE: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated. \u000a \u000aC. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA # REMOVED_CASE_ID , EXCISION: \u000aIsolated tumor cells in one of two lymph nodes (0/2). (See table #2). (See \u000anote). \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #2 \u000aSUMMARY OF SENTINEL LYMPH NODES \u000a \u000aTotal Number of Positive Lymph Nodes: 0 \u000aTotal Number of Lymph Nodes Examined: 2 \u000aNumber with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 1 \u000aNumber with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 0 \u000aNumber with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 0 \u000aMethod of detection: Cytokeratin immunohistochemistry. \u000aExtracapsular Extension: None. \u000aOther Forms Of Axillary Involvement: None \u000a \u000aNOTE: About ten small groups of tumor cells are seen on the pankeratin-stained \u000aslide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, \u000aand pankeratin were examined on tissue levels from each of 3 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Elena F. Brachtel MD*** \u000a \u000aResident Pathologist: \u000aAngela R Shih MD \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000a \u000aQUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER-2/c-erbB-2 \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2 protein. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aHER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is \u000aevaluated visually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The \u000aFDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this \u000alaboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F. Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 09:55*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aNone provided; invasive ductal carcinoma on core biopsy \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT INFERIOR \u000aC: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA # REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 3 containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "right breast needle localized lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE piece of fibroadipose tissue with 2 localization wires in place, a \u000ashort suture denoting the superior margin, and a long suture designating the \u000alateral margin. The long axis of the specimen runs from medial to lateral. The \u000aanterior margin of the specimen is inked blue, the posterior margin black, the \u000asuperior margin green, and the inferior margin yellow. It contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.5cm firm, tan-white mass with ill-defined borders that does not involve the \u000asuperior margin and is located 1.0cm from the closest posterior margin, 1.0cm \u000afrom the closest anterior margin, 0.5cm from the closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and 3.6cm from the medial margin. A coil clip is \u000afound within the mass. The surrounding tissue is soft, yellow, and lobulated, \u000awith focal areas of white fibrous tissue admixed with adipose tissue and a focus \u000aof hemorrhage. The following representative sections are submitted sequentially \u000afrom medial to lateral as follows: \u000a \u000aSECTION CODE: \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial section, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections of fibrous adipose tissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire mass, to include section with the clip and closest inferior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and section with the closest posterior and anterior margins in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margins, serially sectioned. \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "right breast final margin inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.9cm piece of soft, yellow, lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a black \u000asuture designating the final margin, which is inked black. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "right axillary sentinel node # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 0.8cm piece of soft, yellow, lobulated fibroadipose tissue which contains a \u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm lymph node. The lymph node is trisected and entirely \u000asubmitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining fibrofatty tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT \u000aPART B: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT INFERIOR \u000aPART C: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA # REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
