rts,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name \u000aand MR number. \u000aPart A, "#1. Tissue from left breast tissue mammo", consists of 51 g of \u000adisrupted lumpectomy with a whip stitch designated posterior, long stitch \u000adesignated lateral, and short stitch designated superior (medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, superior density of 1.0cm  anterior to posterior 1.6cm ). A wire enters \u000athe specimen from the anterior aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology \u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; \u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The cavity is marked with a clip and is located 0.1cm to the lateral and \u000aposterior margins, 0.5cm to the inferior margin, 1.3cm from the superior and \u000aanterior margins, and 1.9cm to the medial margin. The entire specimen is \u000asubmitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Left breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the area marked with the clip. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains 2 frags in each. \u000aPart B, "#2. Tissue from right breast-mammo", consists of a 31 g lumpectomy \u000a(medial to lateral 4.0cm  superior to inferior 6.2cm  anterior to posterior \u000a1.8cm ). The wire enters the specimen from the lateral and exits at the \u000aanterior aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the \u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned anterior to posterior to reveal a clip located in the area of \u000afibrosis (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm ). The clip is located 1.1cm from the inferior \u000amargin, 2.5cm from the medial margin, 4.1cm from the superior margin, 0.6cm \u000ain the posterior margin, 0.3cm from the lateral margin, and 1.5cm from \u000aanterior margin. The entire specimen is submitted for histology. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Right breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contain the area marked with a clip. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000akst/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday \u000aREMOVED_MONTH 02,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02:57:01PM \u000a[report_end] 
