VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000a55 Fruit Street, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 45) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 09:43 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichele Annette Gadd MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION: \u000a- Metastatic carcinoma in one lymph node (1/1), see synoptic report. \u000a \u000aNote: The largest metastatic focus measures 0.5cm in greatest dimension. An \u000aimmunohistochemical stain for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 was examined on a tissue \u000alevel. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION: \u000a- No carcinoma identified in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 were examined on \u000atissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. RIGHT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000a- Fibrocystic changes. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. RIGHT NIPPLE MARGIN: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aE. LEFT NIPPLE MARGIN: \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunostain for keratin REMOVED_DATE and multiple levels examined. \u000a \u000a \u000aF. LEFT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Invasive ductal carcinoma, multifocal, see synoptic report. \u000a- Ductal carcinoma in-situ. \u000a- Lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000a- Healing biopsy site. \u000a- Fibrocystic changes. \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostains for e-cadherin, keratin REMOVED_DATE  calponin, and p63 were examined \u000aand support the diagnoses. \u000a \u000a \u000aG. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT UPPER OUTER QUADRANT: \u000a- Fibroadipose and scant breast parenchyma. \u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated. \u000a \u000a \u000aH. LYMPH NODE DISSECTION, LEFT AXILLA: \u000a- Metastatic carcinoma in four of fourteen lymph nodes (4/14), see synoptic \u000areport. \u000a- Metastatic carcinoma present in fibroadipose tissue (soft tissue metastasis). \u000a \u000aNote: The largest metastatic focus in a lymph node measures 0.6cm in greatest \u000adimension. A 0.3cm focus of invasive carcinoma is seen in fibroadipose tissue \u000aaway from lymphoid tissue (soft tissue metastasis). \u000a \u000a \u000aI. RIGHT BREAST SKIN EXCISION: \u000a- Skin; no carcinoma identified. \u000a \u000a \u000aJ. LEFT BREAST SKIN EXCISION: \u000a- Skin; no carcinoma identified. \u000a \u000a \u000a================================================================= \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: INVASIVE BREAST CARCINOMA \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: A, F and H \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Left \u000a \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Multiple foci \u000aNumber of Tumor Foci: 3 \u000aTUMOR SIZE (LARGEST): REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm \u000aSIZE(S) OF ADDITIONAL TUMOR FOCI: 1.1cm  0.45cm \u000aGRADE: 1 to 2 \u000aNote: The 1.9cm invasive carcinoma is grade REMOVED_DATE The 1.1cm and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm invasive carcinomas are both grade 1. \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Present, multifocal \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aANTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aPOSTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aNOTE: This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted \u000amargins; please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those r