ECIMEN LATERALITY: Left \u000a \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Multiple foci \u000aNumber of Tumor Foci: Greater than 35 foci, both adjacent to and away \u000afrom the biopsy site \u000aTUMOR SIZE (LARGEST): 0.8cm \u000aNote: Numerous additional foci ranging from <0.1cm to 0.75cm \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Present, multifocal \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aANTERIOR: <0.1cm  over a 0.4cm arc at medial aspect of biopsy cavity \u000aPOSTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000a \u000aLYMPH NODES (NON-SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 3 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 0 \u000a \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Not requested; see prior case  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a**Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD** \u000a \u000aResident Pathologist: \u000aJohn C DeWitt MD, PHD \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aLeft breast cancer. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aC: LEFT BREAST \u000aD: LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS \u000aE: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 5 containers  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh labeled "right subareolar ductal margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm piece of tan-pink soft tissue which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh labeled "left subareolar ductal margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm piece of tan-pink soft tissue which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh labeled "left breast, short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm left mastectomy specimen with a short stitch \u000adesignating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. There is a central \u000aexposed biopsy cavity on the anterior surface measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4.1cm across and \u000a1.3cm in depth. The anterior margin of the specimen, except for the exposed \u000acavity, is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The specimen is \u000asectioned to reveal yellow-tan fatty breast parenchyma with scattered areas of \u000afibrous tissue. The biopsy cavity in the central portion of the specimen comes \u000ato 0.3cm of the black-inked posterior margin and abuts the anterior margin, as \u000apreviously described. At the lateral border of the cavity, the fibrous tissue is \u000afirm and nodular. In addition, immediately medial to the cavity, there is also \u000aan area of firm nodular fibrous tissue with nodules measuring up to 0.3cm in \u000amaximum dimension and lying 0.2cm from the anterior margin and >2cm from the \u000aposterior margin. No lymph nodes are identified, including upon re-examination \u000aof the specimen post-fixation. Specimen reviewed with Dr. Lerwill. Sections are \u000asubmitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sections of firm area medial to cavity, with largest nodule in cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of medial cavity wall to include anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of posterior cavity wall to posterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of inferior cavity wall. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of superior cavity wall. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of lateral cavity wall. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of fibronodular area immediately lateral to cavity \u000ato include posterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of fibrous tissue away from cavity in the lower \u000aouter quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative section of fibrous tissue away from cavity in the lower \u000ainner quadrant. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh labeled "left axillary contents" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm \u000apiece of tan-red fibroadipose tissue containing candidate lymph nodes. The \u000aspecimen is grossly dissected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm area of tan-red \u000afibroadipose tissue, which is bisected to reveal a clip; one half is submitted \u000ain cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the other half submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . One intact \u000alymph node is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the remaining fibroadipose tissue is \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh labeled "right breast, short stitch superior, long stitch \u000alateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm right mastectomy specimen with a short stitch \u000adesignating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The anterior margin \u000ais inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. Specimen is serially \u000asectioned to reveal tan-yellow breast parenchyma with scattered slightly nodular \u000afibrous tissue throughout the specimen. No discrete lesions are seen. Specimen \u000areviewed with Dr. Lerwill. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central. \u000a \u000aGrossed by: \u000aJohn C DeWitt MD, PHD \u000a \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART B: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART C: LEFT BREAST \u000aPART D: LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS \u000aPART E: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
