VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  B. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 52) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 17:58 \u000aResults To: \u000aBarbara Lynn Smith MD, PhD \u000aAmy S. Colwell MD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, LEFT AXILLA #939, EXCISION: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy in two lymph nodes (0/2). (See note). \u000aNOTE: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000apankeratin were examined on tissue levels from each of 2 blocks. The frozen \u000asection diagnosis is confirmed. \u000a \u000aB. BREAST, LEFT, MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Atypical ductal hyperplasia and flat epithelial atypia with calcifications. \u000a- Fibrocystic changes with usual ductal hyperplasia, apocrine cysts and \u000acalcifications. Sclerosing adenosis. \u000a- Fibroadenoma (0.6cm ). \u000a- Healing biopsy site. \u000a \u000aC. BREAST, LEFT AREOLA/NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aLactiferous ducts and breast parenchyma. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aD. BREAST, RIGHT, MASTECTOMY: \u000a- Invasive lobular carcinoma. \u000a- Lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000a- Atypical ductal hyperplasia, focally severely atypical, with calcifications. \u000a- Fibrocystic changes with usual ductal hyperplasia, apocrine cysts and \u000acalcifications. \u000a- Intraductal papillomas. Sclerosing adenosis. \u000a- Two healing biopsy sites. \u000a- See table #1. See note #1. \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA RIGHT BREAST \u000a \u000aTumor Size: Two nodules REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm (gross \u000ameasurements), and several microscopic satellite nodules. \u000aGrade: 2. \u000aLymphatic Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aBlood Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aMargin of Invasive Carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0.1cm \u000afrom the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front (mass #1). \u000aStains for Receptors: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aNOTE #1: The tumor cells are negative for E-cadherin by immunohistochemistry \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The tumor cells in the two nodules are morphologically similar. \u000a \u000aE. BREAST, RIGHT AREOLA-NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aLactiferous ducts. \u000aCauterized intraductal proliferation. \u000a \u000aF. BREAST MARGIN, RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR, EXCISION: \u000aBreast parenchyma and fat. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aG. LYMPH NODES, RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS, DISSECTION: \u000aMetastatic carcinoma in twenty-six of thirty-one lymph nodes (26/31). \u000aSee table #2. See note #2. \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS #2 \u000aSUMMARY OF RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES \u000a \u000aTotal Number of Positive Lymph Nodes: 26. \u000aTotal Number of Lymph Nodes Examined: 31. \u000aNumber with metastases 0.02cm or less (isolated tumor cells): 0. \u000aNumber with metastases >0.02cm to 0.2cm (micrometastases): 3. \u000aNumber with metastases >0.2cm (macrometastases): 23. \u000aExtracapsular Extension: Marked \u000aOther Forms of Axillary Involvement: Soft tissue metastases. \u000aNOTE #2: The metastatic tumor cells appear more pleomorphic than in the breast \u000atumors, with somewhat larger, more hyperchromatic and irregular nuclei. The \u000aresults of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor, progesterone \u000areceptor, and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu protein expression and of fluorescence in-situ \u000ahybridization studies for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification will be reported in an \u000aaddendum ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aH. BREAST MARGIN, RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR TO MASS, EXCISION: \u000aFibroadipose tissue. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Elena F. Brachtel MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000a \u000aQUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is \u000aevaluated visually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The \u000aFDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this \u000alaboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 13:48*** \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000a \u000aQUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS \u000a \u000aLymph Node (Right Axilla, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is \u000aevaluated visually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane \u000aimmunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The \u000aFDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this \u000alaboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 13:47*** \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Quantitation Analyisis \u000a \u000aFLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000aNote: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (188) to \u000achromosome 17 signals (275) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than \u000a2.0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for \u000achromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. \u000a \u000aThe results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be \u000ainterpreted with caution (Equivocal Amplification). \u000aReference: Journal of Clinical Oncology 25:118-145,  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 14:15*** \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Quantitation Analyisis \u000a \u000aFLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION \u000a \u000aLymph Node (Right Axilla, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000aNote: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (181) to \u000achromosome 17 signals (198) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than \u000a2.0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for \u000achromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. \u000a \u000aThe results at or near the cutoff point (ranging from REMOVED_DATE - 2.2) should be \u000ainterpreted with caution (Equivocal Amplification). \u000aReference: Journal of Clinical Oncology 25:118-145,  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F. Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 09:39*** \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1 (SENTINEL NODE LEFT AXILLA #939 & # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): \u000aTwo lymph nodes, negative for metastasis. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aJudith Ann Ferry MD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a52 year old female with right invasive lobular breast cancer, multifocal right \u000aaxillary node positive for cancer on FNA. Left breast biopsy with flat \u000aepithelial atypia. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA #939, EXCISION \u000aB: BREAST, LEFT, MASTECTOMY \u000aC: BREAST, LEFT AREOLA/NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION \u000aD: BREAST, RIGHT, MASTECTOMY \u000aE: BREAST, RIGHT AREOLA//NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION \u000aF: BREAST MARGIN, RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR, EXCISION \u000aG: LYMPH NODES, RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS, DISSECTION \u000aH: BREAST MARGIN, RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR TO MASS, EXCISION \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , MRN \u000a# REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "left axilla sentinel node #939 &  REMOVED_CASE_ID ", are 2 tan-pink lymph \u000anodes, each with scanty amount of attached fatty tissue and each measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a1.3 x 0.8cm  Both the lymph nodes are bisected and frozen entirely, but \u000aseparately as FX#1 & FX#1A, now submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  &  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , \u000arespectively. \u000a \u000aReceived are 7 containers, which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a(JP) \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.0cm \u000anipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior and \u000aa long suture designating lateral. The anterior margin is inked blue and the \u000aposterior margin is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000ahemorrhagic focus with a thin rim of golden-orange tissue containing an M-shaped \u000ametallic clip in the upper outer quadrant located 2.0cm from the anterior \u000amargin and 2.7cm from the posterior margin. The specimen also contains a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5 x 0.4cm grey-white, well-circumscribed, bulging nodule in the upper inner \u000aquadrant, located 1.6cm from the anterior margin and 2.0cm from the posterior \u000amargin, which is separated from hemorrhagic focus by approximately 7.0cm of \u000asoft, lobulated adipose tissue admixed with grey-pink fibrous tissue. The \u000aremaining tissue consists of predominantly soft lobulated adipose tissue admixed \u000awith pink-red, focally cystic fibrous tissue. Lymph nodes are not detected \u000awithin the lateral tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area of clip, upper outer quadrant, to include clip site in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest anterior margin to area of clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest posterior margin to area of clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant nodule, trisected. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest anterior and posterior margin to upper inner quadrant nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved breast tissue. \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "left nipple areola margin", is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm \u000agrey-white fibrofatty tissue, which is inked and submitted in toto in cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.1cm \u000anipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior and \u000aa long stitch designating lateral. The anterior margin is inked blue and the \u000aposterior margin is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm \u000agrey-white, gritty, ill-defined mass (mass #1) in the upper outer quadrant \u000aextending to 0.1cm from the anterior margin and 0.5cm from the posterior \u000amargin. There is an S-shaped clip within the center of the mass. The specimen \u000aalso contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm grey-white, gritty, ill-defined, centrally \u000ahemorrhagic mass (mass #2) in the upper outer quadrant located 1.5cm from the \u000aanterior margin and 2.5cm from the posterior margin, which is separated from \u000amass #1 by approximately 0.3cm of grey-white, granular fibrous tissue. A \u000asecond S-shaped clip is identified within the center of this mass. There are \u000amultiple grey-white firm nodule areas, possibly representing satellite lesions \u000aaveraging 0.2cm  with one measuring up to 0.8cm  The remaining tissue \u000aconsists of soft, lobulated adipose tissue admixed with pink-grey rubbery \u000afibrous tissue. Lymph nodes are not detected within the lateral tissue. \u000aRepresentative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1 to closest anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1 to closest posterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #1 to include area of clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Intervening tissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass #2, to include area of clip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Closest anterior and posterior margins to mass #2. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Satellite nodules. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved. \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "right nipple/areola margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm pink-red fibrofatty tissue, which is inked and submitted in toto in cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "additional anterior margin, right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm aggregate of unremarkable fibrofatty tissues, which are entirely \u000asubmitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aG. Received fresh, labeled "right axillary content", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.3cm \u000aaggregate of yellow lobulated adipose tissue containing multiple tan-pink lymph \u000anodes, ranging from 0.1cm up to 2.9cm in greatest dimension. The lymph nodes \u000aare submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multiple intact lymph nodes per cassette. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One bisected lymph node per cassette. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One serially sectioned lymph node. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One bisected lymph node. \u000a \u000aH. Received fresh, labeled "additional margin anterior to mass, right breast", \u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm aggregate of unremarkable fibrofatty tissues, which are \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA #939, EXCISION \u000aPART B: BREAST, LEFT, MASTECTOMY \u000aPART C: BREAST, LEFT AREOLA/NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION \u000aPART D: BREAST, RIGHT, MASTECTOMY \u000aPART E: BREAST, RIGHT AREOLA//NIPPLE MARGIN, EXCISION \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
