D  LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 of 4 LYMPH NODES. NOTE: The results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODE (LEFT BREAST, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE SEE NOTE. NOTE: The results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation. LYMPH NODE (LEFT, "NONSENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Unfixed, in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "Kathleen Mitchell, REMOVED_DATE  sentinel node, left axilla, hot and blue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing four lymph nodes. The largest lymph node is entirely frozen as FX #1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The other three intact lymph nodes are entirely frozen as FX #1A and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "Kathleen Mitchell, REMOVED_DATE  blue node tail of left breast, # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm piece of fibroadipose containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm blue lymph node, which is entirely frozen as FX#2 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Mitchell, REMOVED_DATE  left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8.0cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect. The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black. The REMOVED_DATE x 9.0cm skin ellipse shows red-purple discoloration encompassing an area of REMOVED_DATE x 6.0cm and extending to the inferior margin. A REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm region in the lateral aspect of the skin has a nodular appearance and extends to 3.0cm from the superior margin, 3.0cm from the inferior margin, and 5.5cm from the lateral tip. The nipple and areola appear unremarkable. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.8cm blood-filled cavity occupies the central region and extends into the outer aspect and to 0.2cm from the posterior margin. The parenchyma surrounding the hematoma shows diffuse fibrosis and hemorrhage. The lower outer quadrant contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  well-circumscribed, tan-pink firm nodule situated 2.5cm inferior to the blood-filled cavity and extending to 2.0cm from the posterior resection margin. The upper outer quadrant contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm  irregular, tan-pink to gray-white, firm mass with a metal clip in the center 2.0cm superior to the blood-filled cavity and extending to 2.5cm from the anterior margin and 1.8cm from the posterior margin. The lower inner quadrant contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm pink-white firm partly cystic mass located 2.3cm from the posterior margin. The remaining parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and pink-white fibrous stroma with areas of hemorrhage. The following representative sections are submitted:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Blood filled cavity with surrounding breast parenchyma from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire lower outer quadrant nodule.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Parenchyma adjacent to the nodule in the lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Mass in the upper outer quadrant with cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing tissue adjacent to the metal clip.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Parenchyma with partly cystic mass in the lower inner quadrant. Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Mitchell, REMOVED_DATE  nonsentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm tan-pink lymph node, which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & #1A; (LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES): FOUR (4) LYMPH NODES WITH NO CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2; (BLUE NODE, TAIL, LEFT BREAST): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE (1) LYMPH NODE. Fellow Review by Ritu Ghai M.D., on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 22,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10:56:07PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 24,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:08:44PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: - The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) - Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) - Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) - The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation; the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: - Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) - Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) - Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 30% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 30,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:15:25PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Nodes (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Lymph Node (Left Breast, "Sentinel"), Excision PART C: Breast (Left), Mastectomy PART D: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Nonsentinel"), Excision PART E: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) PART F: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
