VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 43) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 12:38 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichele Annette Gadd MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000a \u000aRIGHT BREAST: \u000a \u000aD. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID : \u000aNo evidence of malignancy in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels. \u000a \u000aE. BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000a-INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. See Table. \u000a-DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. \u000a-Lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000a-One lymph node with no evidence of malignancy (0/1). \u000a-Fibrocystic changes with apocrine metaplasia and hyalinized fibroadenoma. \u000a-Healing biopsy site. \u000a \u000aTABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000a \u000aTumor Size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm (confirmed microscopically). \u000aGrade: 2. \u000aLymphatic Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aBlood Vessel Invasion: Not identified. \u000aMargin of Invasive Carcinoma: All margins measure greater than 0.2cm  \u000aLocation of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: Within and beyond the region of the mass. \u000aGrade of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: 2. \u000aMargin of Ductal Carcinoma In-Situ: All margins measure greater than 0.2cm  \u000aStains for Receptors: Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aNote: See addendum for results of immunostaining for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu protein \u000aexpression. Also see previous report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  showing invasive tumor positive \u000afor both estrogen and progesterone receptors. Immunostained slides for calponin, \u000asmooth muscle myosin heavy chain and p63 were examined. \u000a \u000aF. BREAST EXCISION MARGIN, RIGHT SUB NIPPLE: \u000a-Lactiferous ducts and breast lobules with no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aLEFT BREAST: \u000a \u000aA. BREAST EXCISION BIOPSY, LEFT TAIL: \u000a-One lymph node with no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aB. BREAST EXCISION MARGIN, LEFT SUB NIPPLE: \u000a-Lactiferous ducts and breast lobules with no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aC. BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000a-Focal flat epithelial atypia. \u000a-Fibrocystic changes with apocrine metaplasia, hyalinized fibroadenoma and \u000aradial scar. \u000a-One lymph node with no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Thomas M Gudewicz MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHER-2 Quantitation by Immunohistochemistry \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aE. BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aThe invasive tumor cells show focal moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2 \u000aprotein. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aHER-2 quantitation: The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated \u000avisually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete \u000amembrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete or incomplete \u000amembrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a> 10% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 12:54*** \u000a \u000aHER-2 FISH Quantitation Analysis \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aE. BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000a \u000aNote: A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene \u000aamplification. \u000a \u000aResults are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals to chromosome 17 \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) signals in 30 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER-2 DNA Probe Kit \u000a(Abbott Molecular Inc.). The average HER-2 copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE and the \u000aaverage  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aResults near the cutoff point (HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2.0) should be interpreted with \u000acaution if the HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is < 2 with the average HER-2 copy number equal \u000ato or greater than 4 and < REMOVED_DATE signals per cell (equivocal amplification). \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F. Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16:01*** \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): \u000aLymph node with no evidence of carcinoma. \u000a \u000aDavid Curtis Wilbur MD \u000a \u000aOther Pathologist(s): \u000aCharlotte I-Wen Wang MD, PhD \u000aAngela R Shih MD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aRight breast cancer; bilateral skin and nipple-sparing simple mastectomy with \u000aright sentinel node biopsy. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION BIOPSY, LEFT TAIL \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION MARGIN, LEFT SUB NIPPLE \u000aC: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aD: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aE: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aF: BREAST EXCISION MARGIN, RIGHT SUB NIPPLE \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 4 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "left tail of breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000atan-pink lymph node with attached yellow soft adipose tissue. The specimen is \u000abisected and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "left subnipple", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm aggregate \u000aof unremarkable tan-yellow portions of fibroadipose tissue, which are submitted \u000ain toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "left breast, short superior, long lateral", is a \u000a13.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm nipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a short suture \u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. There is no \u000aoverlying skin or nipple/areolar complex. The anterior margin of the specimen \u000ais inked blue and the posterior is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5 x 0.4cm lobulated and papilliferous nodule in the upper outer quadrant \u000awhich comes to within 0.2cm of the anterior margin and 1.3cm of the posterior \u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen consists of predominately dense, \u000atan-white, focally cystic fibrous tissue admixed with scant yellow soft adipose \u000atissue. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm tan-pink lymph node is identified within the \u000alateral tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lymph node, bisected. \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "right axillary sentinel \u000anode", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm tan-pink lymph node with attached yellow soft \u000aadipose tissue. The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1 and now \u000asubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aCP \u000a \u000aReceived fresh are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm nipple \u000asparing mastectomy specimen oriented with a short suture designating superior \u000aand a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: \u000aAnterior blue, Posterior black. The specimen contains in the upper outer \u000aquadrant a fine firm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm tan pink nodule with a central embedded \u000ametallic coil clip. The nodule extends to 1.0cm of the anterior surgical \u000amargin. Located lateral to the nodule is a 2nd circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000anodule extending to 0.5cm of the anterior and 2.1cm of the posterior surgical \u000amargins. The remaining cut surfaces are tan pink and fibrous. No lymph nodes \u000aare palpated in the upper outer quadrant. Representative sections are submitted \u000aas follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer nodule with central metallic clip. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant 2nd nodule. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative upper inner breast. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative lower inner breast. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 candidate node. \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "right sub nipple', is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm tan pink \u000asoft tissue, which is submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . JS \u000a \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION BIOPSY, LEFT TAIL \u000aPART B: BREAST EXCISION MARGIN, LEFT SUB NIPPLE \u000aPART C: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aPART D: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aPART E: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
