VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 44) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 19:28 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichele Annette Gadd MD \u000aChien-Wei Eric Liao MD, PhD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA: \u000a- No malignancy identified in 3 lymph nodes (0/3). \u000a \u000aNOTE: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels from each of 3 blocks. \u000a \u000aB. BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000a- Invasive ductal carcinoma, see synoptic report. \u000a- Ductal carcinoma in-situ, extensive, involving multiple quadrants. \u000a- Lobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ). \u000a- Fibrocystic changes. \u000a- Biopsy site changes. \u000a- No malignancy identified in 1 axillary lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aC. SOFT TISSUE EXCISION, LEFT BREAST TAIL: \u000a- Fibroadipose tissue. \u000a \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: Invasive Breast Carcinoma \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: A and B \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Left \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Single focus \u000aTUMOR SIZE: REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aANTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aPOSTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: Present \u000aLOCATION: Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma \u000aGRADE: 2 to 3 \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU \u000aANTERIOR: Positive, focal \u000aPOSTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aCOMMENT: The positive anterior margin is in the lower inner quadrant \u000aLYMPH NODES (SENTINEL AND NON-SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 4 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 0 \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Requested on block(s)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aB. BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aThe invasive tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. \u000aThe invasive tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe invasive tumor cells show focal moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2 \u000aprotein. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2 quantitation: The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated \u000avisually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete or incomplete \u000amembrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) 