CLINICAL HISTORY \u000a44 year old female with left DCIS having mastectomy and SLN biopsy. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA \u000aB: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aC: LEFT BREAST TAIL \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 3 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "left breast axillary \u000asentinel nodes", are three tan-yellow portions of fibroadipose tissue each \u000acontaining a candidate lymph node. The largest node (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm ) is \u000abisected and entirely frozen as FX#1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . A medium-sized lymph \u000anode measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1A, now \u000asubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The smallest lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm is inked \u000ablack, bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1B, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "left breast stitch long lateral, short superior", \u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.8cm mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating \u000asuperior and a long suture designating lateral. The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm tan \u000aportion of skin appears unremarkable and exhibits an unremarkable nipple/areolar \u000acomplex. The anterior margin of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior is \u000ainked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm focus of granular, \u000agritty irregular fibrous tissue, which is focally cystic and hemorrhagic, within \u000athe upper central breast, which comes to 0.1cm of the anterior margin, 3.2cm \u000aof the posterior margin, and contains a ribbon-shaped metallic clip. Also \u000anoted within in this area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm firm tan nodule. The lower \u000ainner breast is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x