. \u000a \u000aNote: Multiple levels examined (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aB. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID : \u000a-No evidence of malignancy in one lymph node (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed. Immunostained slides for \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin were examined on tissue \u000alevels. \u000a \u000aF. SKIN EXCISION, LEFT BREAST: \u000a-Skin with no diagnostic abnormality recognized. \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Thomas M Gudewicz MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION #1; (SENTINEL NODE, RIGHT, # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2; (SENTINEL NODE, LEFT, # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aEugene Jerome Mark MD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aBilateral mastectomy and SLNB, right DCIS (previous lumpectomy with positive \u000amargins x2), left prophylactic. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aB: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aC: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aD: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aE: BREAST MARGIN, RIGHT ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL \u000aF: SKIN EXCISION, LEFT BREAST \u000aG: SKIN EXCISION, RIGHT BREAST \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "sentinel node right \u000aaxilla # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", are 2 tan-pink lymph node candidates, measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1.6cm in \u000agreatest dimension, each with a minimal amount of attached tan-yellow \u000afibroadipose tissue. The smaller lymph node is inked black, and the larger is \u000abisected. The lymph nodes are entirely frozen as FX#1, now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aThe remaining fibroadipose tissue is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "sentinel node left axilla \u000a# REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a 1.5cm in greatest dimension, tan-pink lymph node candidate, with \u000amoderate attached fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is bisected and entirely \u000afrozen as FX#2, now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aReceived are 5 containers, which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.4cm  simple \u000amastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior and a long suture \u000adesignating lateral. There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4.2cm  tan-white portion of \u000askin, which is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm  linear scar. The nipple/areolar \u000acomplex appears unremarkable. The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue \u000aand posterior is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm  \u000atan-white, glistening, stellate focus in the lower-inner quadrant, subjacent to \u000athe previously described scar, and which is 0.8cm from the anterior margin and \u000a2.4cm from the posterior margin. This focus exhibits peripheral tan-yellow, \u000achalky foci, consistent with fat necrosis. The remainder of the specimen \u000aconsists of predominantly dense, tan-white, focally cystic and granular fibrous \u000atissue admixed with yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. Lymph nodes are not \u000adetected in the lateral tissue. Representative sections are submitted as \u000afollows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lesion and surrounding fibrous tissue to include anterior margin. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nearest posterior margin overlying lesion. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper central breast. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer quadrant. \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.3cm  simple \u000amastectomy specimen, with a short suture designating superior and long suture \u000adesignating lateral. The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4.1cm  nipple/areolar complex appears \u000aunremarkable. The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue and the \u000aposterior is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  \u000ahemorrhagic cavity in the upper-outer quadrant, which is 1.4cm from the \u000aanterior margin and 0.7cm from the posterior margin. The cavity is surrounded \u000aby dense, tan-white fibrous tissue, which exhibits focal, chalky, yellow areas, \u000aconsistent with fat necrosis. The remainder of the specimen consists of \u000apredominantly dense, tan-white, focally cystic and granular fibrous tissue \u000aadmixed with yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. Lymph nodes are not detected in \u000athe lateral tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Hemorrhagic cavity, upper-outer quadrant, and surrounding fibrous \u000atissue. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nearest anterior margin overlying hemorrhagic cavity. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-inner quadrant. \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "right breast, additional superficial margin", is a \u000a5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  aggregate of irregular, tan-yellow portions of fibroadipose \u000atissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "left breast skin ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  \u000atan-white portion of skin. Representative sections are submitted in cassette \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aG. Received fresh, labeled "right breast skin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm \u000aaggregate of irregular tan-white portions of skin. Representative sections are \u000asubmitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . 