om the posterior \u000amargin, 0.6cm from the superior margin, 0.6cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and 1.2cm from the inferior margin. The \u000asurrounding tissue consists of tan-yellow, focally hemorrhagic, lobulated \u000aadipose tissue and scant gray-white, rubbery tissue. The specimen is entirely \u000aand sequentially submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , as \u000afollows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin en face. \u000a \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:53:20AM \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final \u000aDiagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed \u000aor corrected the diagnoses. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aADDENDUM NOTE: \u000aREASON: #1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR \u000aRECEPTOR PROTEINS \u000a \u000aBreast (Right, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): \u000aThe ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen \u000areceptor protein. \u000aThe ductal carcinoma in-situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone \u000areceptor protein. \u000aSee note. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aThese tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by \u000athe Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not \u000abeen cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The \u000aFDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this \u000alaboratory has established and verified the test?s accuracy and precision. \u000a \u000a \u000aAddendum #1 by Atul K Bhan M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH \u000a13,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12:31:14PM \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final \u000aDiagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed \u000aor corrected the diagnoses. \u000a \u000aPART : Breast (Right), Excision \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
