t tissue fragment, which is dissected and palpated to reveal 1 candidate lymph node, which is bisected and submitted entirely for Frozen Section as FX #2, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1; (SENTINEL NODE # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2; (LEFT AXILLA, NODE # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 17,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:52:33PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Right, Subareolar Margin), Excision PART B: Breast (Left, Subareolar Margin), Excision PART C: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART D: Breast (Right, Additional Margin), Excision PART E: Breast (Left, Additional Margin), Excision PART F: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART G: Lymph Node (Ri [report_end] 
