VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-07- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS: \u000aColumnar cell change with flat epithelial atypia, associated with mucin \u000aproduction. \u000aRadial sclerosing lesion with adjacent core biopsy site. \u000aApocrine metaplasia. \u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium. \u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen, \u000aincluding margins. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: A 49-year-old postmenopausal female with abnormal right mammogram \u000astatus post right breast core Bx on REMOVED_DATE revealing fragments of a radial \u000asclerosing lesion WLE Bx. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, \u000awhipstitch on deep margin to mammo. \u000aRADIOLOGY: \u000aCalcifications and intact hookwire are within the specimen. \u000aNo clip is present. \u000aSignature: Dr. Gombos \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name, unit number, \u000aand "#1. R breast tissue stitches - short superior, long lateral, whip deep \u000amargin", consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, \u000aoriented by sutures designating superior (short suture), lateral (long suture) \u000aand deep (whipstitch) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol \u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; \u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing \u000awire enters the anterior/superior aspect of the specimen, and exits the \u000ainferior/posterior surface. Specimen is received with an accompanying \u000aradiograph demonstrating a localizing wire in place within the specimen, \u000amarking a small focus of microcalcifications. Sectioning in this area \u000ademonstrates a 1.0cm focus of firm dense fibrous tissue, with a 0.5cm \u000apalpably firm nodule abutting the posterior margin. Fibrous tissue radiates to \u000athe superior, anterior, posterior, medial and lateral margins. Nodule focally \u000aabuts the posterior and medial margins, is 0.5cm from the nearest superior \u000amargin, 0.7cm from the nearest anterior margin and 1.5cm from the nearest \u000alateral margin and remote from the inferior margin. Remaining specimen shows \u000adense white fibrous tissue (60-70% of parenchyma), without additional \u000adefinitive lesions or other abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen is \u000asubmitted, sequentially from superior to inferior, with perpendicular superior \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and perpendicular inferior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Palpable nodule (? \u000aprior biopsy site) is submitted in micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen, sequentially from superior to inferior, multi \u000afrags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000adb/elw \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on \u000a4/3/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
