 end of the specimen, 5.3cm superior to the cyst, 0.5cm from the anterior margin, abutting the posterior margin, abutting the superior margin, 4.8cm to the inferior margin, abutting the medial margin, & 0.1cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the parenchyma is unremarkable. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Superior margin, enface.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Inferior margin, radial.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remainder of specimen entirely submitted serially, superior to inferior. The following cassettes contain 1 section divided into 2 pieces:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  &  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , each cassette also contains the hemorrhagic cyst and calcifications. Received in formalin, labeled "left mass", is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of breast, which is inked black. The specimen consists of yellow-pink-white, fatty to rubbery tissue, without any abnormalities. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with tips in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , enface, with true margin up. Final Diagnosis by Ritu Ghai M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 26,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11:33:43AM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Breast (Left mass), Excision [report_end] 
