D \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a18 year old female with fibroepithelial neoplasms. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT #2 \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT #1 \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NODULE #1 \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NODULE #2 \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 4 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "right breast final margin #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm piece of yellow-white fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin, which is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "right breast final margin #1", are two pieces of \u000ayellow-white fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.4cm  each with a suture designating the final margin, which is inked black. \u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "right breast nodule #1", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.2cm \u000apiece of breast with needle localization wire. The specimen is inked black. It \u000acontains a poorly circumscribed, tan-white firm to rubbery mass, measuring REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.2 x 2.2cm  The mass abuts the inked margin focally. The remaining breast \u000aparenchyma consists predominately of dense fibrous tissue with scanty amount of \u000afatty tissue. The mass contains a metallic clip. Representative sections are \u000asubmitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the end margins \u000aand cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the section containing the metallic clip. \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "right breast nodule #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm \u000apiece of breast with needle localization wire. The specimen is inked black. It \u000acontains a poorly circumscribed, tan-white, lobulated firm to rubbery mass, \u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm  The mass extends up to the inked margin focally. \u000aThere is scanty amount of remaining breast parenchyma which is mostly fibrous. \u000aSubmitted entirely and sequentially from one end margin to the opposite end \u000amargin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the end margins. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT #2 \u000aPART B: BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN, RIGHT #1 \u000aPART C: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NODULE #1 \u000aPART D: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NODULE #2 \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
