VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000a55 Fruit Street, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 59) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 16:04 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichelle Connolly Specht MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000a \u000aA: BREAST, RIGHT, BIOPSY: \u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, single focus, present less than 0.1cm from the \u000ainked margin. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia, several microscopic foci. \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000a \u000aNote: Multiple levels examined ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000aB: BREAST, RIGHT, EXCISION: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, grade 2, 0.9cm in greatest dimension, present \u000agreater than 0.2cm from the inked margin (see synoptic report). \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present at \u000aor less than 0.2cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia, several microscopic foci. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aCalcifications. \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000a \u000aC: BREAST, RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aCalcifications. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000a \u000aNote: Multiple levels examined. ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The resection margins of the specimen(s) \u000awere inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aD: BREAST, RIGHT INFERIOR MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, 2 foci in adjacent blocks (probably contiguous), \u000agrade 2, 0.2cm in greatest dimension; greater than 0.2cm from the inked margin. \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aCalcifications. \u000a \u000aNote: To evaluate for invasive carcinoma, immunostained slides for calponin, \u000asmooth muscle myosin heavy chain, p63, and cytokeratin were examined. The \u000afindings support the diagnosis ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). The resection margins of the specimen(s) \u000awere inked and microscopically evaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aE: BREAST, RIGHT DEEP MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, single focus, 0.15cm in greatest dimension, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin. \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aCalcifications. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aF: BREAST, RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.1cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia, scattered microscopic foci. \u000aBackground of dense stromal fibrosis. \u000aCalcifications. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000aG: SENITNEL LYMPH NODE, RIGHT AXILLA, EXCISION: \u000aLymph node with no evidence of carcinoma (0/1). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were \u000aexamined on tissue levels from 2 blocks with unique tissue. \u000a \u000aH: BREAST, RIGHT LATERAL MARGIN, EXCISION: \u000aLobular neoplasia (lobular carcinoma in-situ), abundant, multifocal, present \u000aless than 0.2cm from the inked margin in multiple foci. \u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified. \u000a \u000aNote: The resection margins of the specimen(s) were inked and microscopically \u000aevaluated; see individual gross descriptions. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: INVASIVE BREAST CARCINOMA \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: B, D, E and G \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Right \u000a \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Multiple foci \u000aNumber of Tumor Foci: 3 \u000aTUMOR SIZE (LARGEST): 0.9cm \u000aSIZE(S) OF ADDITIONAL TUMOR FOCI: 0.2cm  0.15cm \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aINKED MARGIN: <0.1cm  focal and IN SPECIMEN E (DEEP MARGIN) \u000aNOTE: This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted \u000amargins; please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results. \u000a \u000aLYMPH NODES (SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 1 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 0 \u000a \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Requested on block(s)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By David Curtis Wilbur MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aB. BREAST, RIGHT, EXCISION: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed at MGH on formalin fixed tissue with the \u000afollowing results for \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA: \u000a \u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR Positive (>90%, strong staining) \u000a \u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR Negative (0) \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN Negative (1+) \u000a \u000a \u000aNOTE: \u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  protein are evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following \u000acriteria. \u000a \u000aEstrogen and Progesterone Receptor Analysis: Estimation of nuclear \u000aimmunoreactivity of tumor cells. \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Analysis: \u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or minimal immunoreactivity in < 10% of \u000atumor cells. \u000aNegative (1+): Faint immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a \u000aportion of the membrane is positive. \u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate incomplete membrane (Focal 2+) or complete \u000amembrane (2+) immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aEquivocal (2-3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a>10% of tumor cells. \u000aPositive (3+): Strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor \u000acells. \u000a \u000aExternal and internal controls are evaluated and show appropriate \u000aimmunoreactivity. Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative \u000aresult.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  IHC results are often complemented by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH analysis, which is \u000areported as a separate addendum. \u000a \u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests \u000aperformed at Massachusetts General Hospital were developed and their performance \u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the \u000aDepartment of Pathology at MGH. They have not been cleared or approved by the \u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such \u000aclearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000aReferences: \u000aHammond MEH et al: ASCO/CAP Testing Guideline Recommendations for \u000aImmunohistochemical Testing of Estrogen and Progesterone Receptors in Breast \u000aCancer. DOI: 10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /JCO. REMOVED_CASE_ID .25. REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aWolff AC Et al: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing in Breast Cancer Guideline Update. DOI: \u000a10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /apra. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID -SA. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16:45*** \u000a \u000aADDENDUM \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000a \u000aImmunostains for keratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were evaluated on 2 additional blocks both \u000astains support the interpretation already rendered ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: David Curtis Wilbur MD on REMOVED_DATE 11:11*** \u000a \u000aHER-2 FISH Quantitation Analysis \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aB. BREAST, RIGHT, EXCISION: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000a \u000aNote: A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene \u000aamplification. \u000a \u000aResults are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals to chromosome 17 \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) signals in 30 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER-2 DNA Probe Kit \u000a(Abbott Molecular Inc.). The average HER-2 copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE and the \u000aaverage  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aResults near the cutoff point (HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2.0) should be interpreted with \u000acaution if the HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is < 2 with the average HER-2 copy number equal \u000ato or greater than 4 and < REMOVED_DATE signals per cell (equivocal amplification). \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 15:53*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aBreast cancer. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST BIOPSY, RIGHT \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT INFERIOR MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT DEEP MARGIN \u000aF: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN \u000aG: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA \u000aH: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT LATERAL MARGIN \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . (HG) \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh, labeled "right breast needle localized biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a3.5 x 2.5cm piece of breast with needle localization wire. The margins are \u000adisrupted focally and show a defect measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  The specimen is \u000ainked black. It contains an irregularly outlined red, hemorrhagic cavity filled \u000awith blood clot measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm and extending up to the closest \u000ablack-inked margin. The breast parenchyma surrounding the cavity is hemorrhagic \u000aand indurated. In the remaining area, the breast parenchyma consists of admixed \u000afatty tissue and dense pink-white fibrous stroma which is granular focally. An \u000aobvious mass is not identified. Representative sections are submitted from one \u000aend margin to the opposite end margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000arepresenting the end margins, cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing sections of the \u000abreast parenchyma with hemorrhagic cavity and cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing \u000asections immediately adjacent to the metallic clip. \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "right breast needle localized lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm piece of yellow-white breast with needle localization wire. The \u000aspecimen was previously partially incised. The specimen is carefully inked \u000ablack. The breast parenchyma consists of admixed fatty tissue and dense \u000apink-white fibrous stroma which is nodular and rubbery focally. The breast \u000aparenchyma also shows hemorrhage focally. The diffuse fibrosis extends from one \u000aend margin to the opposite end margin and measures 7.0cm in greatest dimension. \u000aA metallic clip is not identified. Representative sections are submitted in \u000acassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the end margins and \u000acassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the area denoted by the needle localization wire. \u000a \u000aReceived fresh are 6 containers, A-H which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , \u000a# REMOVED_CASE_ID . (JS) \u000a \u000aC. Labeled, "right breast margin superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm \u000afibroadipose tissue oriented with a suture on one broad surface designating the \u000anew final margin. The new final margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned \u000aand submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Labeled, "right breast margin inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm tan-pink \u000afibroadipose tissue oriented with a suture on one broad surface designating the \u000anew final margin. The new final margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned \u000aand submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Labeled, "right breast margin deep", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm tan-pink \u000afibrous tissue oriented with a suture on one broad surface designating the new \u000afinal margin. The new final margin is inked and the specimen is serially \u000asectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aF. Labeled, "right breast margin medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm tan-pink \u000afibrous tissue oriented with a suture on one broad surface designating the new \u000afinal margin. The new final margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned and \u000asubmitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aG. Labeled, "right axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm \u000afibroadipose tissue with a 2.8cm in maximum dimension candidate lymph node. \u000aDissection shows yellow glistening fibrofatty surfaces. The specimen is \u000asubmitted entirely as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Node. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Remaining fat. \u000a \u000aH. Labeled, "right breast margin lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.8cm fibroadipose \u000atissue oriented with a suture on one broad surface designating the new final \u000amargin. The new final margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned and \u000asubmitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aGrossed by: \u000aJohn Shushereba \u000aHimanshu Gunderia \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST BIOPSY, RIGHT