tions of tan wrinkled skin with underlying fibrofatty soft tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm to 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and appears unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received in formalin, labeled "right breast skin", are 3 irregularly-shaped unremarkable tan wrinkled fragments of skin ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm to REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1.3cm  The underlying fibrofatty soft tissue is serially sectioned and appears unremarkable. Representative sections of each fragment are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION # 1 AND #1A; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY #372): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2 AND #2A; (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE #[335]): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 01,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03:25:45PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right axilla), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Simple Mastectomy PART C: Breast (Left), Simple Mastectomy PART D: Lymph Node (Left Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART E: Skin (left breast), Excision PART F: Skin (right), Excision PART G: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) PART H: Cryostat Frozen [report_end] 
