 involvement: None BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISION: MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. EXTENSIVE FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. BREAST (RIGHT, "INFERIOR MARGIN"), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). SEE NOTE. NOTE: The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E-cadherin. The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Michaud, REMOVED_DATE  right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm piece of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire, a short suture designating the superior aspect, and a long suture designating the lateral aspect. The superior margin is inked blue, the inferior margin black, the medial margin green, and the lateral margin yellow. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm indurated area with an eccentric hemorrhagic focus. In it is a metal clip. This area extends to 0.1cm from the inferior margin, 0.2cm from the medial margin, 0.3cm from the lateral margin, 1.0cm from the superior margin, 0.7cm from the anterior margin, and 1.4cm from the posterior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted from posterior to anterior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the posterior margin en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the anterior margin en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the indurated area with the clip in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Michaud, REMOVED_DATE  right breast inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.2cm piece of gray-white to tan-pink fibrofatty tissue with a suture along one aspect, which is inked. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Michaud, REMOVED_DATE  left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.0cm piece of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue with a short suture designating the superior aspect, a long suture designating the lateral aspect, and three localization wires. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior margin blue, the medial margin green, and the lateral margin yellow. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm indurated gray-white area, which extends to 0.2cm from the medial margin, 0.4cm from the posterior margin, 1.7cm from the anterior margin, 1.7cm from the lateral margin, and greater than 2cm from the superior and inferior margins. Surrounding this area is focal hemorrhage. Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the superior end en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , the inferior end en face in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , and the entire indurated nodule in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Unfixed, labeled "Kathleen Michaud, REMOVED_DATE  left axillary contents", is a REMOVED_DATE x 8 x 1.5cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue containing lymph nodes from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm to REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0.4cm  The lymph nodes are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Four whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Three whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Three whole lymph nodes.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single bisected lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single bisected lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single bisected lymph node.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single whole lymph node. Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #1: QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) to strong (3+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) HER-2/c-erbB-2 quantitation: The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows: Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) Show strong (3+) over overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Addendum #1 by Elena F Brachtel M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE: REASON #2: RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals (732) to chromosome 17 signals (111) in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Results at or near the 