or cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe invasive tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2 protein. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2 quantitation: The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated \u000avisually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete or incomplete \u000amembrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 15:42*** \u000a \u000aHER-2 FISH Quantitation Analysis \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aA. BREAST CORE BIOPSY, RIGHT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). \u000a \u000aNote: A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene \u000aamplification. \u000a \u000aResults are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals to chromosome 17 \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER-2 DNA Probe Kit \u000a(Abbott Molecular Inc.). The average HER-2 copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE and the \u000aaverage  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aResults near the cutoff point (HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2.0) should be interpreted with \u000acaution if the HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is < 2 with the average HER-2 copy number equal \u000ato or greater than 4 and < REMOVED_DATE signals per cell (equivocal amplification). \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 15:34*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000a52 y.o. F w/ hypoechoic mass in the right breast. ? IDC vs ILC vs radial scar. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST CORE BIOPSY, RIGHT \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. BREAST CORE BIOPSY, RIGHT: Received in formalin,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME 's name \u000a& MRN ( REMOVED_CASE_ID ) & "Right Breast", are 6 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging \u000afrom REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000a \u000aPART : BREAST CORE BIOPSY, RIGHT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
