VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Updated \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000aBoston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  H. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 52) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: PAC \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 15:19 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichele Annette Gadd MD \u000a \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: \u000aInvasive mammary carcinoma with mixed ductal and lobular features. \u000aLobular carcinoma in-situ, classic and non-classic (florid and pleomorphic) \u000atypes. \u000aFlat epithelial atypia. \u000aFibrocystic changes and columnar cell change with calcifications. \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000aSee synoptic report (at the end of report) and note. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunohistochemical stain shows the invasive carcinoma is negative for \u000aE-cadherin throughout, suggestive of lobular type; however, based on the degree \u000aof tubule formation, the tumor is classified as mixed ductal and lobular type. \u000aIt is too atypical for tubulolobular type. The in-situ carcinoma is also \u000anegative for E-cadherin, supporting lobular carcinoma in-situ (LCIS). There are \u000aa few foci of pleomorphic LCIS in the region of the mass and not at the margin. \u000aIn this excision and in the final margin specimens below, there is also \u000aflorid-type LCIS characterized by marked distension of involved ducts. In the \u000afinal margin specimens, there is also LCIS with increased cytologic atypia, but \u000afalling short of pleomorphic type. The clinical significance of these \u000avariant/non-classic forms of LCIS beyond that of classic LCIS, particularly in \u000athe setting of invasive carcinoma, is unknown. Therefore, the clearance to the \u000afinal margins is omitted. \u000a \u000aB. RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION: \u000aTwo lymph nodes with no evidence of malignancy (0/2). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels from each of 2 blocks. \u000a \u000aC. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION, LATERAL FINAL MARGIN: \u000aLobular carcinoma in-situ, present throughout the tissue, focally florid-type. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunohistochemical stain for E-cadherin is negative, supporting LCIS. \u000aFlorid LCIS is not identified at the margin. \u000a \u000aD. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION, INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN: \u000aLobular carcinoma in-situ, present throughout the tissue, focally florid-type. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunohistochemical stain for E-cadherin is negative, supporting LCIS. \u000aFlorid LCIS is not identified at the margin. \u000a \u000aE. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION, MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN: \u000aLobular carcinoma in-situ, present throughout the tissue, with focal increased \u000acytologic atypia. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunohistochemical stain for E-cadherin is negative, supporting LCIS. \u000aLCIS with increased atypia is not identified at the margin. \u000a \u000aF. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION, SUPERIOR FINAL MARGIN: \u000aLobular carcinoma in-situ, present throughout the tissue, including foci of \u000aflorid-type and with increased cytologic atypia. \u000aFibrocystic changes. \u000a \u000aNote: An immunohistochemical stain for E-cadherin is negative, supporting LCIS. \u000aFlorid LCIS and LCIS with increased atypia are not identified at the margin. \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: Invasive Breast Carcinoma \u000a \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: A and B \u000a \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Right \u000a \u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aTUMOR FOCALITY: Single focus \u000aTUMOR SIZE: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm \u000aNote: Gross measurement, and supported by tumor in multiple contiguous \u000atissue sections. \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000aNote: Scored 2 for tubules, 3 for atypia, and 1 for mitotic activity, for \u000aoverall grade 2. \u000aLYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000aBLOOD VESSEL INVASION: Not identified \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA \u000aINKED MARGIN: Less than 0.1cm  focal \u000aNOTE: This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted \u000amargins; please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results. \u000a \u000aLYMPH NODES (SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 2 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 0 \u000a \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Requested ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  only) on block(s)  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aNOTE: See prior report,  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , for results of hormone receptor studies. \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By Kristina M Braaten MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHER-2 Quantitation by Immunohistochemistry \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aThe invasive tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2 protein. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aHER-2 quantitation: The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated \u000avisually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete \u000amembrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete or incomplete \u000amembrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in \u000a> 10% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 13:30*** \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aRight breast mass, BIRADS 4, invasive lobular carcinoma. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT \u000aB: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA \u000aC: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aF: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT SUPERIOR FINAL MARGIN \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aA. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID  & "right needle localized \u000alumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm unoriented piece of breast with a partially \u000adetached localization wire, which is inked black. The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x \u000a2.0 x 1.3cm  gray-white, ill-defined, lobulated mass with focal hemorrhage \u000asurrounding a coiled metallic clip which abuts the inked margin. The mass is \u000aextremely ill-defined, with multiple possible satellite lesions or continuations \u000aof the mass. The remaining tissue consists of grey-white, fibrous tissue with \u000aminimal fat. Representative sections are submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : End margin, en face. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : 1 section from each slice sequentially, to include mass to closest \u000amargin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : End margin, en face. \u000a \u000aReceived are 5 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . (CP) \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "right axillary sentinel node", are 2 irregular \u000atan-pink lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm & REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  The \u000aspecimen is entirely submitted as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One lymph node, bisected. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One lymph node, bisected. \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh, labeled "right breast margin lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm irregular, focally ragged tan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with 2 \u000asutures designating the final margin which is inked black. The specimen is \u000aentirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh, labeled "right breast margin inferior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin which is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh, labeled "right breast margin medial", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin which is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh, labeled "right breast margin superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan-yellow portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture designating the final \u000amargin which is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000a \u000a \u000aPART A: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT \u000aPART B: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA \u000aPART C: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN \u000aPART D: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN \u000aPART E: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
