VAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Specht, Michelle \u000a \u000aMassachusetts General Hospital \u000a55 Fruit Street, Boston, MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel (617) REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aSurgical Pathology Report \u000a \u000a \u000aAccession #:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  S. \u000aDOB: REMOVED_DATE (Age: 49) \u000aSex: F \u000aMRN:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aLocation: MGH  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aInstitution: MGH \u000aDate of Operation: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDate of Accession: REMOVED_DATE \u000aReported: REMOVED_DATE 08:39 \u000aResults To: \u000aMichelle Connolly Specht MD \u000aChien-Wei Eric Liao MD, PHD \u000a \u000aFINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA: \u000aNo evidence of carcinoma in four lymph nodes (0/4). \u000aImmunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined \u000aon tissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000aB. BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aDuctal carcinoma in-situ, nuclear grade 2, involving 8 of 12 blocks. \u000aDCIS is present less than 0.1cm from anterior margin focally ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ). \u000aHealing biopsy site. \u000aSee synoptic report. \u000a \u000a \u000aD. BREAST EXCISION, LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aE. BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000a \u000aF. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA: \u000aNo evidence of carcinoma in two lymph nodes (0/2). \u000aImmunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined \u000aon tissue levels from 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a================================================================= \u000a \u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU \u000aPARTS INCLUDED: A and C \u000aSPECIMEN LATERALITY: Right \u000a \u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU \u000aSIZE: Involving 8 of 12 blocks \u000aGRADE: 2 \u000a \u000aDISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU \u000aANTERIOR: <0.1cm  focal \u000aPOSTERIOR: 0.2cm or greater \u000aNOTE: This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted \u000amargins; please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results. \u000a \u000aLYMPH NODES (SENTINEL) \u000aTOTAL NUMBER EXAMINED: 4 \u000aTOTAL NUMBER WITH CARCINOMA: 0 \u000a \u000aANCILLARY STUDIES \u000aRECEPTOR STUDIES: Not requested; see prior case  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000a \u000a**Electronically Signed Out By Amy Ly MD** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE): \u000aNo carcinoma identified in one lymph node. \u000a \u000aAmy Ly MD \u000a \u000aOther Pathologist(s): \u000aAngela R Shih MD \u000aKrzysztof Glomski MD, PHD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aDCIS of breast, right, grade 2. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA \u000aB: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aC: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aD: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aE: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aF: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 6 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab labeled "right axillary sentinel \u000alymph node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm lymph node with abundant attached fat. The \u000alymph node is bisected and frozen entirely as FX#1, now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remaining \u000afat is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh labeled "right subareolar ductal margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.3cm piece of tan-yellow soft tissue that is submitted in toto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aC. Received fresh labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm \u000anipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior, and \u000aa long suture designating lateral. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the \u000aposterior margin inked black. The specimen contains a diffuse area of granular \u000afibrous tissue spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.1cm in the central-outer to upper-outer \u000abreast. No clip is seen. The surrounding tissue is yellow-white, fibrofatty \u000awith focal fibrocystic change. No lymph nodes are seen in the lateral tissue. \u000aThe following representative sections are submitted: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative sections from the central-outer to upper-outer breast \u000asequentially from medial to lateral. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Uninvolved breast. \u000a \u000aD. Received fresh labeled "left subareolar ductal margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan-red soft tissue that is submitted in toto in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aE. Received fresh labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.3cm \u000anipple-sparing mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating superior, and \u000aa long suture designating lateral. The anterior margin is inked blue, and the \u000aposterior margin inked black. The specimen consists of yellow-white, fibrofatty \u000atissue with scattered cysts measuring up to 1.5cm and containing straw-colored \u000afluid. No discrete masses or lesions are seen. No lymph nodes are seen in the \u000alateral tissue. The following representative sections are submitted: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper-inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-inner quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower-outer quadrant. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Central breast. \u000a \u000aF. Received fresh labeled "left axillary sentinel node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm \u000apiece of fat containing two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm and REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5 x 0.5cm  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows: \u000a \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Larger lymph node, bisected. \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Smaller lymph node bisected. \u000a \u000aGrossed by: \u000aDerek Kingman \u000a \u000aImmunohistochemical and in-situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts \u000aGeneral Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics \u000adetermined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of \u000aPathology at Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or \u000aapproved by the U.S.Food and Drug Administration (FDA); the FDA has determined \u000athat such clearance or approval is not necessary. \u000aPART A: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA \u000aPART B: BREAST EXCISION, RIGHT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART C: BREAST MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aPART D: BREAST EXCISION, LEFT NIPPLE / SUBAREOLAR MARGIN \u000aPART E: BREAST MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000a \u000a \u000a[report_end] 
