 block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aNote: One section shows blue ink on a cut surface of tumor after rereview of \u000athe gross specimen and submission of additional material for microscopic review \u000ait is determined that this represents carryover ink and is not indicative of \u000amarginal involvement by tumor. \u000a \u000a \u000aC. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT: \u000aBreast parenchyma with fibrocystic changes including abundant usual ductal \u000ahyperplasia and focal flat epithelial atypia and lobular neoplasia (atypical \u000alobular hyperplasia). \u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia. \u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy. \u000a \u000aD. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #412: \u000aLymph nodes (2) with no evidence of carcinoma (0/2). \u000a \u000aNote: Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and \u000acytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels from each of 2 blocks. \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By David Curtis Wilbur MD*** \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aBy his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis \u000acertifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or \u000acorrected the diagnosis. \u000a \u000a \u000aPROCEDURES/ADDENDA \u000a \u000aHormone Receptor Quantitation \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aB. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000aThe invasive tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein. \u000aThe invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. \u000aThe invasive tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2 protein. \u000a \u000aNote: \u000aEstrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation: The percent of immunoreactive \u000anuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows: \u000a- The tumor cells stain (> 10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Some tumor cells stain (1 to <10% of nuclei stained) \u000a- Rare tumor cells stain (< 1% of nuclei stained) \u000a- The tumor cells do not stain (0% of nuclei stained) \u000a \u000aHER-2 quantitation: The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated \u000avisually and reported as follows: \u000a- Do not show overexpression (0 to 1+, no/minimal immunoreactivity or \u000aincomplete membrane staining of tumor cells) \u000a- Show moderate (2+) overexpression (weak to moderate complete or incomplete \u000amembrane immunoreactivity in > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a- Show strong (3+) overexpression (strong complete membrane immunoreactivity \u000ain > 10% of tumor cells) \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Atul K Bhan MBBS, MD on REMOVED_DATE 13:34*** \u000a \u000aHER-2 FISH Quantitation Analysis \u000aOrdered Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aB. BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT: \u000aBlock tested:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a \u000aHER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Amplified). \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000aNote: A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates HER-2/neu gene \u000aamplification. \u000a \u000aResults are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 signals to chromosome 17 \u000a( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) signals in 30 tumor cell nuclei using PathVysion by HER-2 DNA Probe Kit \u000a(Abbott Molecular Inc.). The average HER-2 copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE and the \u000aaverage  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  copy number/cell is REMOVED_DATE \u000a \u000aResults near the cutoff point (HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio 2.0) should be interpreted with \u000acaution if the HER-2/ REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ratio is < 2 with the average HER-2 copy number equal \u000ato or greater than 4 and < REMOVED_DATE signals per cell (equivocal amplification). \u000a \u000aReference: ASCO/CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update, Arch Pathol Lab Med. \u000adoi:10. REMOVED_CASE_ID /arpa. REMOVED_CASE_ID - REMOVED_CASE_ID .SA \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a \u000a***Electronically Signed Out By: Elena F. Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 18:08*** \u000a \u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS \u000aFROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE # REMOVED_CASE_ID ): \u000aNo carcinoma identified, await sentinel workup. \u000a \u000aThomas M Gudewicz MD \u000a \u000aOther Pathologist(s): \u000aNicholas A Zane MD, PhD \u000aMonica C Chung MD \u000aDipti P Sajed MD, PhD \u000a \u000aCLINICAL HISTORY \u000aRight breast cancer. \u000a \u000aSPECIMENS SUBMITTED: \u000aA: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, RIGHT AXILLA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aB: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, RIGHT \u000aC: BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, LEFT \u000aD: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION, LEFT AXILLA #412 \u000a \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION \u000aReceived are 4 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , # REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000a \u000aA. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled "right axillary sentinel \u000anode # REMOVED_CASE_ID ", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm piece of fat containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and frozen entirely as FX#1, now as \u000a REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . The remainder of the specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000a \u000aB. Received fresh, labeled "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7.2cm mastectomy \u000aspecimen with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating \u000alateral. The REMOVED_DATE x 2.5cm nipple and areola appear unremarkable. The anterior \u000amargin is inked blue and the posterior margin inked black. The specimen \u000acontains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm stellate, indurated, tan-pink mass in the \u000acentral-lower inner breast that is 3.3cm from the posterior margin and 